{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZuNhkqDrtn5CabcziqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I can now proceed to the design phase:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add an `OrderStatus` enum with values `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED`. Add a `status` field to the `Order` data class, initialized to `ACTIVE` by default in creation flows.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt**: Add two new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` — when a CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancellation (409 response)\n   - `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CREATED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` — when attempting to create a shipment for a cancelled order (409 response)\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add a `findByOrderIdFilteredByStatus(orderId: String, status: OrderStatus)` method, but actually, I'll simplify: just add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Order>` or leverage the fact that orderId is unique. Actually no, I need to find **shipments** by orderId, not orders. So ShipmentRepository needs this.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the `create` method, after checking if the shipment already exists, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If it is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with the new error code.\n\n6. **OrderController.kt**: Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order; if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`\n   - If already CANCELLED, return the order (idempotent)\n   - If ACTIVE, check if any shipment is CONFIRMED; if yes, throw `ConflictException` with `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and don't save anything\n   - If all shipments are CREATED or none exist, change order status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save order and shipments, return the order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an active order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling already-cancelled order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling when shipment is CONFIRMED fails with 409\n   - Cancelling non-existent order fails with 404\n   - Created shipments under cancelled order are cancelled\n   - All-or-nothing on confirmation conflict\n\n**Rejected alternative:**\nI considered using a service layer to handle the cancellation logic, but the existing codebase has controllers directly using repositories without service classes. To stay consistent with the existing architecture, I'll keep the logic in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order with CREATED shipments**:\n   - Read: Order from repository, all Shipments by orderId\n   - Check: Order exists (404 if not), no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any)\n   - Write: Order status to CANCELLED, all CREATED Shipments status to CANCELLED\n   - Return: Updated Order with status CANCELLED\n\n2. **Cancel already-cancelled order**:\n   - Read: Order from repository\n   - Check: Order exists (404 if not)\n   - Action: No changes, return order as-is (idempotent)\n   - Return: Order with status CANCELLED\n\n3. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment**:\n   - Read: Order, Shipments\n   - Check: CONFIRMED shipment found\n   - Action: Throw 409, nothing changes\n   - Return: Error response\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order**:\n   - Read: Order lookup fails\n   - Action: Throw 404\n   - Return: Error response\n\n5. **Create shipment for cancelled order**:\n   - Read: Order by orderId\n   - Check: Order exists (keep current behavior if not), order is not CANCELLED\n   - Action: Throw 409 if CANCELLED\n   - Return: Error response (409) if CANCELLED\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancelActiveOrderSucceeds` — Create order, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED and response code is 200\n2. `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent` — Create order, cancel it, cancel again, verify succeeds\n3. `cancelOrderWithConfirmedShipmentFails` — Create order, create shipment, confirm it, attempt cancel, verify 409 and nothing changed\n4. `cancelNonExistentOrderFails` — Attempt cancel on non-existent order, verify 404\n5. `cancelOrderCancelledCreatedShipments` — Create order with multiple shipments (some CREATED, some CONFIRMED), cancel and verify only CREATED are cancelled\n6. `createShipmentForCancelledOrderFails` — Create order, cancel it, attempt create shipment, verify 409\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1233,"cache_read_input_tokens":22468,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1233},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94d75db5-65e7-4fc0-91ff-a6f68444aa3c","uuid":"c313a2fe-cd35-4f96-b0cb-500d0b74fe2c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:01:31.989Z","request_id":"req_011CfZuNgkoztaPMwR3PyQc7"}
