{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZuX8aoRNJTXMAz9C18D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 21 tests pass. The command output shows:\n- **Tests run: 21, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0**\n- **BUILD SUCCESS**\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — All 21 tests pass, including 3 pre-existing customer controller tests and 1 application test\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — The 4 original OrderControllerTest tests and all 5 ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint** — Implemented in OrderController, cancels active orders, persists state, cancels CREATED shipments\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent** — Uses existing ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) with error codes in ApiError envelope\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds** — Test `cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent` verifies idempotency\n   ✅ **Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing** — Test `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing` verifies all-or-nothing semantics\n   ✅ **Unknown order refused** — Test `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` verifies 404 response\n   ✅ **Shipment for cancelled order refused** — Test `rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409` verifies rejection\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only touched Kotlin source files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified order/shipment feature files and api package\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status` field to Order data class with default ACTIVE. This is necessary to track order lifecycle.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CREATED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` error codes. These are required to distinguish different failure scenarios in the API contract.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to retrieve all shipments for an order. This is necessary for the cancel operation to find and update related shipments.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection and check to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders. This enforces the business rule that cancelled orders cannot accept new shipments.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** — Added ShipmentRepository injection and implemented `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with full logic: existence check, idempotency, CONFIRMED shipment blocking (all-or-nothing), and status/shipment updates.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new test cases:\n   - `newly created order has ACTIVE status` — Verifies default status\n   - `cancels an active order and returns CANCELLED status` — Verifies successful cancellation\n   - `cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent` — Verifies idempotent behavior\n   - `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — Verifies not-found handling\n   - `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing` — Verifies all-or-nothing semantics\n   - `cancelling an order cancels all CREATED shipments but not CANCELLED ones` — Verifies shipment status updates\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection, reset in @BeforeEach, and 2 new test cases:\n   - `rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409` — Verifies business rule enforcement\n   - `allows creating a shipment for a non-existent order` — Verifies backward compatibility (orders don't need to exist beforehand)\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All ticket requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), preventing cancellations when shipments are CONFIRMED, and preventing shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `Order.kt`: Added OrderStatus enum and status field (default ACTIVE)\n- `ApiError.kt`: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CREATED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt`: Added findByOrderId(orderId) method\n- `ShipmentController.kt`: Added order cancellation check when creating shipments\n- `OrderController.kt`: Added cancel endpoint with idempotency, all-or-nothing semantics, and shipment updates\n- `OrderControllerTest.kt`: Added 6 tests for cancel endpoint behavior\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt`: Added 2 tests for cancelled order shipment handling\n\n**Tests:**\n- `newly created order has ACTIVE status` — Verifies order initialization\n- `cancels an active order and returns CANCELLED status` — Verifies successful cancellation\n- `cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent` — Verifies retry safety\n- `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — Verifies error handling\n- `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing` — Verifies all-or-nothing constraint\n- `cancelling an order cancels all CREATED shipments but not CANCELLED ones` — Verifies cascading updates\n- `rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409` — Verifies business rule\n- `allows creating a shipment for a non-existent order` — Verifies backward compatibility\n\n**Verification:** Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ directory. Result: **21 tests passed (10 order + 7 shipment + 3 customer + 1 app), 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**\n\n**Not done:** Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2459,"cache_read_input_tokens":40836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2459},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],